      <Comment source="PMN, zhang, SRI, caspi">A dihydroflavonol is |FRAME: Flavones| hydroxylated at C3 and lacking the double bond between carbons 2 and 3. The name is misleading, since the absence of the double bond makes it |FRAME: Flavanols| rather than |FRAME: Flavonols|.</Comment>
